1
00:00:10,501 --> 00:00:16,181
Love is a song that never ends

2
00:00:16,181 --> 00:00:22,021
Life may be swift and fleeting

3
00:00:22,141 --> 00:00:27,541
Hope may die
Yet love's beautiful music

4
00:00:27,621 --> 00:00:33,261
Comes each day like the dawn

5
00:00:33,341 --> 00:00:38,861
Love is a song that never ends

6
00:00:38,901 --> 00:00:44,701
One simple theme repeating

7
00:00:44,741 --> 00:00:50,461
Like the voice of a heavenly choir

8
00:00:50,541 --> 00:00:57,101
Love's sweet music flows on

9
00:01:04,421 --> 00:01:10,021
Like the voice of a heavenly choir

10
00:01:10,821 --> 00:01:16,101
Love's sweet music flows on

11
00:03:17,421 --> 00:03:19,021
(FRIEND OWL SNORING)

12
00:03:39,301 --> 00:03:40,861
(BABY BIRDS CHIRPING)

13
00:04:19,381 --> 00:04:22,061
(BIRD WHISTLING)

14
00:04:47,461 --> 00:04:48,861
THUMPER: Wake up.

15
00:04:48,941 --> 00:04:50,021
(THUMPER THUMPING)

16
00:04:50,101 --> 00:04:52,901
-(GROANING) What now?
-THUMPER: Wake up, Friend Owl.

17
00:04:52,941 --> 00:04:55,141
(EXCLAIMING)
What's going on around here?

18
00:04:55,221 --> 00:04:57,541
-Wake up.
-It's happened.

19
00:04:57,621 --> 00:04:59,581
The new prince is born.

20
00:04:59,621 --> 00:05:03,101
-We're going to see him.
-Come on. You better hurry up.

21
00:05:13,341 --> 00:05:15,141
(ANIMALS GASPING SOFTLY)

22
00:05:16,101 --> 00:05:18,101
ANIMAL 1: Well, look.

23
00:05:19,981 --> 00:05:22,941
ANIMAL 2: Well.
ANIMAL 3: Isn't he cute?

24
00:05:26,741 --> 00:05:30,301
Well, this is quite an occasion.

25
00:05:31,301 --> 00:05:35,261
Yes, sir,
it isn't every day a prince is born.

26
00:05:37,461 --> 00:05:39,141
You're to be congratulated.

27
00:05:39,181 --> 00:05:42,981
ANIMAL 1: Yes, congratulations.
ANIMAL 2: Congratulations.

28
00:05:43,461 --> 00:05:45,221
Thank you very much.

29
00:05:45,701 --> 00:05:49,421
Come on. Wake up. We have company.

30
00:05:55,221 --> 00:05:56,981
ANIMAL 3: Hello. Hello, there.

31
00:05:57,061 --> 00:06:00,221
-ANIMAL 1: Hello, little prince.
-Hello. Hello, there.

32
00:06:00,301 --> 00:06:02,061
Hello, little prince.

33
00:06:03,061 --> 00:06:05,301
(FRIEND OWL HOOTING)

34
00:06:10,661 --> 00:06:13,021
(FRIEND OWL LAUGHING)

35
00:06:16,381 --> 00:06:19,141
(LAUGHING)

36
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:23,821
Look. He's trying to get up.

37
00:06:46,701 --> 00:06:48,941
Kinda wobbly, isn't he?

38
00:06:49,021 --> 00:06:50,461
Thumper.

39
00:06:52,181 --> 00:06:54,181
Well, he is.

40
00:06:55,901 --> 00:06:57,541
Aren't you?

41
00:06:57,701 --> 00:06:59,541
(EXCLAIMING)

42
00:07:00,941 --> 00:07:03,221
(ALL LAUGHING)

43
00:07:05,141 --> 00:07:08,421
Looks to me like
he's getting kind of sleepy.

44
00:07:11,741 --> 00:07:14,261
I think it's time we all left.

45
00:07:14,301 --> 00:07:15,981
FRIEND OWL: Come on. (SHOOING)

46
00:07:18,381 --> 00:07:19,821
(SHOOING)

47
00:07:23,381 --> 00:07:24,741
(SHOOING)

48
00:07:33,421 --> 00:07:36,101
MRS. HARE:
Thumper. Come on.

49
00:07:39,061 --> 00:07:41,141
Whatcha gonna call him?

50
00:07:41,781 --> 00:07:46,061
Well, I think I'll call him Bambi.

51
00:07:46,461 --> 00:07:47,941
(ENUNCIATING)

52
00:07:49,941 --> 00:07:53,061
Yep, I guess that'll do all right.

53
00:07:53,781 --> 00:07:54,941
Bambi.

54
00:07:55,981 --> 00:07:57,981
My little Bambi.

55
00:08:19,901 --> 00:08:21,741
(WHISTLING)

56
00:08:28,141 --> 00:08:31,621
Walking already.
Well, what do you know.

57
00:08:42,981 --> 00:08:46,021
(QUAIL WHISTLING)

58
00:08:47,741 --> 00:08:50,701
-Good morning.
-Good morning, Mrs. Quail.

59
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:53,661
And where's the young prince this... Oh!

60
00:08:56,181 --> 00:08:59,621
-Good morning, Bambi.
-Good morning, young prince.

61
00:09:02,861 --> 00:09:04,181
Goodbye.

62
00:09:07,861 --> 00:09:10,021
MRS. POSSUM:
Good morning, young prince.

63
00:09:16,461 --> 00:09:18,461
Good morning, young prince.

64
00:09:32,901 --> 00:09:34,301
Good morning.

65
00:09:34,381 --> 00:09:35,981
Hmm.

66
00:09:36,061 --> 00:09:37,621
Nice sunny day.

67
00:09:49,941 --> 00:09:52,061
-What's the matter?
-What happened?

68
00:09:52,101 --> 00:09:55,061
Did the young prince fall down?

69
00:09:55,141 --> 00:09:58,581
-Is he hurt?
-No, he's all right.

70
00:10:00,461 --> 00:10:03,061
He doesn't walk very good, does he?

71
00:10:03,181 --> 00:10:05,061
MRS. HARE: Thumper.

72
00:10:06,101 --> 00:10:07,461
Yes, Mama?

73
00:10:08,781 --> 00:10:11,941
What did your father tell you
this morning?

74
00:10:14,741 --> 00:10:17,861
If you can't say something nice,

75
00:10:21,101 --> 00:10:24,141
don't say nothing at all.

76
00:10:25,861 --> 00:10:29,661
Come on, Bambi, get up. Try again.

77
00:10:29,741 --> 00:10:32,581
Come on, get up. Get up.

78
00:10:32,621 --> 00:10:34,621
-Get up.
-Try again.

79
00:10:43,621 --> 00:10:45,741
(LAUGHING)

80
00:10:55,221 --> 00:10:57,301
(LAUGHING)

81
00:11:06,061 --> 00:11:09,981
I'm thumping.
That's why they call me Thumper.

82
00:11:10,021 --> 00:11:11,821
(ECHOING)

83
00:11:12,901 --> 00:11:14,901
Thumper! (ECHOING)

84
00:11:32,701 --> 00:11:35,861
Come on. You can do it.

85
00:11:36,701 --> 00:11:39,661
Hop over it. Like this.

86
00:11:41,061 --> 00:11:44,181
Hop over it.

87
00:11:46,341 --> 00:11:47,741
Like this.

88
00:11:56,501 --> 00:11:59,021
(LAUGHING)

89
00:12:00,781 --> 00:12:03,221
You didn't hop far enough.

90
00:12:06,621 --> 00:12:09,181
That's it. Now the other one.

91
00:12:19,701 --> 00:12:22,941
Gee whiz, what happened that time?

92
00:12:23,701 --> 00:12:26,141
(BIRDS WHISTLING)

93
00:12:40,781 --> 00:12:42,781
Those are birds.

94
00:12:44,661 --> 00:12:47,301
(REPEATING)

95
00:12:47,981 --> 00:12:50,261
Look, he's trying to talk.

96
00:12:52,661 --> 00:12:54,661
He's trying to say "bird."

97
00:12:57,061 --> 00:12:59,061
Say "bird."

98
00:12:59,981 --> 00:13:01,661
(REPEATING)

99
00:13:02,701 --> 00:13:04,501
(ENUNCIATING) Bird.

100
00:13:04,581 --> 00:13:05,701
(REPEATING)

101
00:13:07,021 --> 00:13:08,461
Uh-uh.

102
00:13:09,021 --> 00:13:10,941
Bird.

103
00:13:10,981 --> 00:13:13,421
Come on, say "bird," say "bird."

104
00:13:13,461 --> 00:13:16,501
Say "bird." Say "bird."
Come on, say "bird."

105
00:13:16,581 --> 00:13:18,581
Say "bird."

106
00:13:20,701 --> 00:13:22,141
Bird.

107
00:13:22,221 --> 00:13:24,261
(ALL LAUGHING)

108
00:13:24,261 --> 00:13:27,381
He talked. He talked, Mama.

109
00:13:27,461 --> 00:13:29,861
The young prince said "bird."

110
00:13:29,941 --> 00:13:32,821
Bird, bird, bird...

111
00:13:52,301 --> 00:13:53,661
Bird.

112
00:13:53,701 --> 00:13:55,901
No, that's not a bird.

113
00:13:55,981 --> 00:13:58,221
That's a butterfly.

114
00:13:58,301 --> 00:14:00,501
Butterfly?

115
00:14:00,541 --> 00:14:01,901
Butter...

116
00:14:06,341 --> 00:14:08,181
Butterfly.

117
00:14:08,181 --> 00:14:10,781
(LAUGHING) No, that's a flower.

118
00:14:10,821 --> 00:14:14,581
-Flower?
-Uh-huh. It's pretty.

119
00:14:15,501 --> 00:14:17,501
(SNIFFING)

120
00:14:20,021 --> 00:14:21,341
Pretty.

121
00:14:22,061 --> 00:14:23,741
(SNIFFING)

122
00:14:29,061 --> 00:14:30,901
Flower.

123
00:14:30,981 --> 00:14:32,461
Me?

124
00:14:32,501 --> 00:14:34,021
(THUMPER LAUGHING)

125
00:14:37,421 --> 00:14:39,701
No, no, no, no.

126
00:14:40,981 --> 00:14:43,581
That's not a flower.

127
00:14:43,661 --> 00:14:46,341
-He's a little...
-Oh, that's all right.

128
00:14:46,381 --> 00:14:51,221
He can call me a flower if he wants to.

129
00:14:53,461 --> 00:14:55,381
(LAUGHING SHYLY)

130
00:14:55,461 --> 00:14:57,901
I don't mind.

131
00:15:01,821 --> 00:15:04,341
Pretty. Pretty flower.

132
00:15:06,821 --> 00:15:09,061
Oh! (LAUGHING)

133
00:15:10,901 --> 00:15:12,301
Gosh.

134
00:15:17,101 --> 00:15:19,381
(THUNDER CRASHING)

135
00:15:23,861 --> 00:15:27,301
I think I better go home now.

136
00:16:23,781 --> 00:16:26,221
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

137
00:16:26,301 --> 00:16:28,981
Beating a tune
As you fall all around

138
00:16:29,021 --> 00:16:31,621
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

139
00:16:31,661 --> 00:16:34,301
What can compare
With your beautiful sound?

140
00:16:34,341 --> 00:16:37,141
Beautiful sound
Beautiful sound

141
00:16:37,181 --> 00:16:39,461
Drip, drop
Drip, drop

142
00:16:39,541 --> 00:16:42,101
Drip, drip, drop
When the sky is cloudy

143
00:16:42,141 --> 00:16:44,701
Your pretty music
Can brighten the day

144
00:16:44,781 --> 00:16:47,301
Drip, drip, drop
When the sky is cloudy

145
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:50,021
You come along
with a song right away

146
00:16:50,101 --> 00:16:51,981
Come with your beautiful music

147
00:16:52,061 --> 00:16:54,661
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

148
00:16:54,741 --> 00:16:57,381
Beating a tune
As you fall all around

149
00:16:57,461 --> 00:16:59,981
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

150
00:17:00,101 --> 00:17:02,621
What can compare
With your beautiful sound?

151
00:17:02,661 --> 00:17:05,261
Drip, drip, drop
When the sky is cloudy

152
00:17:05,341 --> 00:17:08,101
You come along
With your pretty little song

153
00:17:08,181 --> 00:17:10,381
Drip, drip, drop
When the sky is cloudy

154
00:17:10,461 --> 00:17:12,861
You come along
With your pretty little song

155
00:17:12,941 --> 00:17:15,421
-Gay little roundelay
-Gay little roundelay

156
00:17:15,501 --> 00:17:18,021
-Song of the rainy day
-Song of the rainy day

157
00:17:18,101 --> 00:17:20,581
How I love to hear your patter
Pretty little pitter-patter

158
00:17:20,701 --> 00:17:23,341
Helter skelter, when you pelter
Troubles always seem to scatter

159
00:17:23,381 --> 00:17:25,781
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

160
00:17:25,861 --> 00:17:28,661
Beating a sound as you fall all around

161
00:17:28,701 --> 00:17:30,941
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

162
00:17:31,021 --> 00:17:33,901
-Little April shower
-With your beautiful sound

163
00:17:59,341 --> 00:18:00,981
(THUNDER CRASHING)

164
00:18:02,741 --> 00:18:05,181
(WIND HOWLING)

165
00:18:59,941 --> 00:19:02,101
(WHISTLING)

166
00:19:06,301 --> 00:19:09,141
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

167
00:19:09,181 --> 00:19:11,741
Beating a tune
As you fall all around

168
00:19:11,781 --> 00:19:14,421
Drip, drip, drop
Little April shower

169
00:19:14,461 --> 00:19:17,061
What can compare
With your beautiful sound?

170
00:19:17,141 --> 00:19:20,181
Beautiful sound

171
00:19:52,181 --> 00:19:55,021
Mother, what we going to do today?

172
00:19:55,101 --> 00:19:57,661
I'm going to take you to the meadow.

173
00:19:58,141 --> 00:20:01,221
Meadow? What's the meadow?

174
00:20:01,301 --> 00:20:04,181
It's a very wonderful place.

175
00:20:04,261 --> 00:20:07,181
Then why haven't we
been there before?

176
00:20:07,221 --> 00:20:09,861
You weren't big enough.

177
00:20:09,941 --> 00:20:12,661
-Mother, you know what?
-What?

178
00:20:12,701 --> 00:20:15,821
We're not the only deer in the forest.

179
00:20:15,861 --> 00:20:19,301
-Where did you hear that?
-Thumper told me.

180
00:20:19,381 --> 00:20:21,341
Well, he's right.

181
00:20:21,381 --> 00:20:24,021
There are many deer in the forest
besides us.

182
00:20:24,101 --> 00:20:26,621
Then why don't I ever see them?

183
00:20:26,701 --> 00:20:29,741
-You will, sometime.
-On the meadow?

184
00:20:29,821 --> 00:20:31,581
Perhaps.

185
00:20:31,661 --> 00:20:32,981
Hush now.

186
00:20:34,901 --> 00:20:36,621
We're almost there.

187
00:20:46,501 --> 00:20:48,501
-(HAPPILY) The meadow.
-Wait.

188
00:20:48,901 --> 00:20:51,101
Bambi, wait.

189
00:20:52,821 --> 00:20:55,741
You must never rush out
on the meadow.

190
00:20:55,781 --> 00:20:57,781
There might be danger.

191
00:20:58,701 --> 00:21:01,221
Out there, we're unprotected.

192
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:03,741
The meadow is wide and open,

193
00:21:03,821 --> 00:21:06,421
and there are no trees or bushes
to hide us.

194
00:21:06,501 --> 00:21:08,821
So we have to be very careful.

195
00:21:10,181 --> 00:21:11,821
Wait here.

196
00:21:12,781 --> 00:21:18,101
I'll go out first.
And if the meadow is safe, I'll call you.

197
00:22:02,141 --> 00:22:04,261
(WHISTLING)

198
00:22:09,461 --> 00:22:12,461
Come on, Bambi. It's all right.

199
00:22:16,821 --> 00:22:18,301
Come on.

200
00:22:56,581 --> 00:22:58,341
(EXCLAIMING)

201
00:23:09,741 --> 00:23:11,861
RABBITS: Good morning, Prince Bambi.

202
00:23:11,901 --> 00:23:14,381
MRS. HARE:
Good morning, young prince.

203
00:23:14,461 --> 00:23:17,221
Hello. What ya eatin'?

204
00:23:17,261 --> 00:23:20,421
-Clover.
-It's awfully good.

205
00:23:20,501 --> 00:23:22,501
It's delicious.

206
00:23:22,541 --> 00:23:25,061
Why don't you try some?

207
00:23:27,661 --> 00:23:31,061
No, not that green stuff.

208
00:23:31,581 --> 00:23:33,821
Just eat the blossoms.

209
00:23:33,901 --> 00:23:35,901
That's the good stuff.

210
00:23:37,301 --> 00:23:38,661
MRS. HARE: Thumper.

211
00:23:40,061 --> 00:23:44,061
-Yes, Mama?
-What did your father tell you?

212
00:23:44,501 --> 00:23:46,021
About what?

213
00:23:46,061 --> 00:23:50,141
About eating the blossoms
and leaving the greens?

214
00:23:50,541 --> 00:23:52,541
Oh, that one.

215
00:23:53,261 --> 00:23:54,581
(CLEARING THROAT)

216
00:23:54,661 --> 00:23:58,421
Eating greens is a special treat.

217
00:23:58,461 --> 00:24:02,661
It makes long ears and great big feet.

218
00:24:03,941 --> 00:24:07,941
But it sure is awful stuff to eat.

219
00:24:09,021 --> 00:24:11,941
I made that last part up myself.

220
00:24:15,621 --> 00:24:18,741
Watch out.

221
00:24:30,061 --> 00:24:32,061
(SNIFFING)

222
00:24:45,661 --> 00:24:47,981
(FALINE GIGGLING)

223
00:25:20,981 --> 00:25:23,501
That's little Faline.

224
00:25:24,461 --> 00:25:27,421
He's kind of bashful, isn't he, Mama?

225
00:25:27,501 --> 00:25:31,261
ENA: Well, maybe he wouldn't be
if you'd say hello.

226
00:25:34,901 --> 00:25:36,501
Hello, Bambi.

227
00:25:40,701 --> 00:25:43,221
I said hello.

228
00:25:43,301 --> 00:25:45,661
Well, aren't you going to answer her?

229
00:25:48,861 --> 00:25:51,021
You're not afraid, are you?

230
00:25:54,341 --> 00:25:56,421
Well, then, go ahead.

231
00:26:02,581 --> 00:26:04,581
Go on, say hello.

232
00:26:08,701 --> 00:26:09,861
Hello.

233
00:26:09,981 --> 00:26:12,021
(GIGGLING)

234
00:26:17,701 --> 00:26:19,541
(SPLASH)

235
00:26:26,501 --> 00:26:28,581
(FALINE LAUGHING)

236
00:26:48,221 --> 00:26:50,021
(ANGRILY) You.

237
00:29:26,261 --> 00:29:28,821
He stopped and looked at me.

238
00:29:28,901 --> 00:29:31,061
Yes, I know.

239
00:29:31,501 --> 00:29:35,581
Why was everyone still
when he came on the meadow?

240
00:29:35,621 --> 00:29:37,981
Everyone respects him.

241
00:29:38,061 --> 00:29:43,941
For of all the deer in the forest,
not one has lived half so long.

242
00:29:44,581 --> 00:29:48,421
He's very brave and very wise.

243
00:29:49,621 --> 00:29:54,861
That's why he's known as
the Great Prince of the Forest.

244
00:30:36,141 --> 00:30:38,421
(CROWS CAWING)

245
00:31:01,861 --> 00:31:03,061
Faline.

246
00:31:06,581 --> 00:31:07,821
Bambi.

247
00:31:10,221 --> 00:31:11,701
Mother.

248
00:31:14,661 --> 00:31:18,021
Bambi.

249
00:31:23,821 --> 00:31:25,541
Mother.

250
00:31:41,021 --> 00:31:42,901
(GUNS FIRING)

251
00:31:42,981 --> 00:31:45,101
(CROWS CAWING)

252
00:32:05,741 --> 00:32:07,621
Come on out, Bambi.

253
00:32:10,181 --> 00:32:11,541
Come on.

254
00:32:12,581 --> 00:32:14,101
It's safe now.

255
00:32:14,701 --> 00:32:17,181
We don't have to hide any longer.

256
00:32:19,701 --> 00:32:23,381
What happened, Mother?
Why did we all run?

257
00:32:27,421 --> 00:32:31,381
Man was in the forest.

258
00:34:12,021 --> 00:34:15,901
Mother, look.
What's all that white stuff?

259
00:34:17,061 --> 00:34:19,541
Why, it's snow.

260
00:34:19,821 --> 00:34:22,141
-Snow?
-Yes.

261
00:34:22,221 --> 00:34:23,541
Winter has come.

262
00:34:53,981 --> 00:34:56,261
(ICE TINKLING)

263
00:34:56,341 --> 00:34:57,781
(THUMPING)

264
00:35:04,261 --> 00:35:05,581
(ICE TINKLING)

265
00:35:28,101 --> 00:35:30,261
THUMPER: Hiya, Bambi.

266
00:35:30,901 --> 00:35:33,021
Watch what I can do.

267
00:35:36,341 --> 00:35:38,381
(WHOOPING)

268
00:35:48,981 --> 00:35:51,701
Come on. It's all right.

269
00:35:51,781 --> 00:35:53,181
Look.

270
00:35:54,021 --> 00:35:56,021
The water's stiff.

271
00:36:11,981 --> 00:36:14,821
Some fun, huh, Bambi?

272
00:36:17,541 --> 00:36:20,101
Come on, get up. Like this.

273
00:36:39,541 --> 00:36:41,501
(LAUGHING) No, no, no.

274
00:37:00,981 --> 00:37:03,741
Kinda wobbly, aren't you?

275
00:37:13,181 --> 00:37:14,901
(CLEARING THROAT)

276
00:37:24,941 --> 00:37:28,501
Got to watch both ends
at the same time.

277
00:37:34,381 --> 00:37:36,581
Guess you better unwind it.

278
00:38:02,501 --> 00:38:04,181
(EXCLAIMING)

279
00:38:19,621 --> 00:38:22,421
(FLOWER SNORING)

280
00:38:31,461 --> 00:38:34,261
Wake up. Wake up, Flower.

281
00:38:37,821 --> 00:38:40,741
Is it spring yet?

282
00:38:41,301 --> 00:38:43,981
No. Winter's just started.

283
00:38:44,661 --> 00:38:47,301
What you doing? Hibernating?

284
00:38:49,941 --> 00:38:51,981
Uh-huh.

285
00:38:53,261 --> 00:38:55,541
What do you want to do that for?

286
00:38:57,141 --> 00:39:01,021
(CHUCKLING)
All us flowers sleep in the winter.

287
00:39:04,661 --> 00:39:08,581
Well, good night.

288
00:39:12,941 --> 00:39:14,821
(SIGHING)

289
00:40:14,581 --> 00:40:16,581
(SIGHING)

290
00:40:17,941 --> 00:40:21,301
Winter sure is long, isn't it?

291
00:40:21,381 --> 00:40:22,981
It seems long.

292
00:40:24,061 --> 00:40:26,581
But it won't last forever.

293
00:40:31,101 --> 00:40:33,301
I'm awful hungry, Mother.

294
00:40:33,381 --> 00:40:35,661
Yes, I know.

295
00:40:45,101 --> 00:40:46,741
Bambi, come here.

296
00:40:47,981 --> 00:40:49,141
Look.

297
00:40:50,621 --> 00:40:52,981
New spring grass.

298
00:41:16,501 --> 00:41:18,341
Bambi. Quick.

299
00:41:18,421 --> 00:41:19,821
The thicket.

300
00:41:22,341 --> 00:41:23,941
(GUNSHOT)

301
00:41:24,981 --> 00:41:27,461
Faster. Faster, Bambi.

302
00:41:28,141 --> 00:41:31,381
Don't look back. Keep running.

303
00:41:31,461 --> 00:41:33,541
Keep running.

304
00:41:35,901 --> 00:41:37,621
(GUNSHOT)

305
00:41:45,661 --> 00:41:47,861
We made it. (PANTING)

306
00:41:47,941 --> 00:41:49,661
We made it, Mother.

307
00:41:50,661 --> 00:41:51,981
We...

308
00:41:52,741 --> 00:41:54,061
Mother.

309
00:41:58,221 --> 00:41:59,981
Mother!

310
00:42:06,421 --> 00:42:08,821
Mother, where are you?

311
00:42:13,701 --> 00:42:15,301
Mother!

312
00:42:20,501 --> 00:42:22,261
Mother!

313
00:42:24,221 --> 00:42:25,541
Mother!

314
00:42:32,021 --> 00:42:33,661
Mother!

315
00:42:42,261 --> 00:42:44,221
Mother! (CRYING)

316
00:42:46,061 --> 00:42:47,381
(GASPING)

317
00:42:49,461 --> 00:42:52,221
Your mother can't be
with you anymore.

318
00:43:08,701 --> 00:43:10,301
Come.

319
00:43:11,581 --> 00:43:12,861
My son.

320
00:43:29,741 --> 00:43:32,421
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

321
00:43:35,781 --> 00:43:38,381
Let's sing a gay little spring song

322
00:43:39,301 --> 00:43:42,061
This is the season to sing

323
00:43:42,101 --> 00:43:45,901
So I'd like to suggest
That we all do our best

324
00:43:45,941 --> 00:43:48,941
And warble a song about spring

325
00:43:49,021 --> 00:43:51,461
Spring, spring, spring

326
00:43:51,541 --> 00:43:53,741
Let's get together and sing

327
00:43:58,541 --> 00:44:01,301
Let's sing a gay little spring song

328
00:44:02,221 --> 00:44:05,141
Just like the bird on the wing

329
00:44:05,181 --> 00:44:08,701
Things always seem right
When you're cheerful and bright

330
00:44:08,781 --> 00:44:11,461
So let's get together and sing

331
00:44:11,541 --> 00:44:14,141
Sing, sing, sing

332
00:44:14,221 --> 00:44:17,501
Let's sing a song about spring

333
00:44:17,581 --> 00:44:21,021
Let's twitter and tweet
Like the birdies in May

334
00:44:21,101 --> 00:44:24,421
Get into the mood
And be merry today

335
00:44:24,461 --> 00:44:26,941
Forget all your troubles
And warble away...

336
00:44:26,981 --> 00:44:28,221
(SNORING)

337
00:44:28,301 --> 00:44:29,421
Wait.

338
00:44:30,061 --> 00:44:32,061
(GROANING) What now?

339
00:44:34,301 --> 00:44:36,341
Hey.

340
00:44:37,461 --> 00:44:39,141
Stop that racket.

341
00:44:39,221 --> 00:44:40,421
Scat.

342
00:44:40,821 --> 00:44:42,341
(SHOOING)

343
00:44:42,421 --> 00:44:44,981
Let's sing a song about spring

344
00:44:46,101 --> 00:44:47,661
I'll fix 'em.

345
00:44:48,661 --> 00:44:50,261
(HOOTING SOFTLY)

346
00:44:51,821 --> 00:44:52,981
(HOOTING LOUDLY)

347
00:44:55,141 --> 00:44:59,661
(PANTING) There.
I guess that'll teach 'em.

348
00:45:01,181 --> 00:45:03,181
(BIRDS WARBLING)

349
00:45:04,301 --> 00:45:06,901
Oh, what's the use?

350
00:45:09,901 --> 00:45:12,581
This is the season to sing...

351
00:45:16,461 --> 00:45:19,021
Same thing every spring.

352
00:45:21,141 --> 00:45:23,381
(MIMICKING WARBLING BIRDS)

353
00:45:26,421 --> 00:45:28,741
Love's sweet song.

354
00:45:30,421 --> 00:45:33,061
Pain in the pin feathers, I call it.

355
00:45:53,741 --> 00:45:54,861
Stop it.

356
00:45:58,421 --> 00:46:00,621
Get out of here. All of you.

357
00:46:03,581 --> 00:46:05,141
And you, too.

358
00:46:06,621 --> 00:46:10,421
Hello, Friend Owl.
Don't you remember me?

359
00:46:10,461 --> 00:46:12,741
Why, it's the young prince.

360
00:46:13,141 --> 00:46:14,501
Bambi!

361
00:46:16,101 --> 00:46:18,701
My, my, how you've changed.

362
00:46:18,741 --> 00:46:21,621
Turn round there. Let me look at you.

363
00:46:21,701 --> 00:46:25,421
I see you've traded in your spots
for a pair of antlers.

364
00:46:28,661 --> 00:46:33,981
You know, just the other day
I was talking to myself about you.

365
00:46:34,061 --> 00:46:36,861
And we were wondering
what had become of you.

366
00:46:36,941 --> 00:46:38,941
THUMPER: Hello, Bambi.

367
00:46:40,421 --> 00:46:41,981
Remember me?

368
00:46:43,181 --> 00:46:44,261
Thumper.

369
00:46:45,421 --> 00:46:46,661
Right.

370
00:46:46,981 --> 00:46:49,061
(LAUGHING)

371
00:46:51,301 --> 00:46:53,301
Hi, fellas.

372
00:46:53,781 --> 00:46:55,101
Flower.

373
00:46:55,941 --> 00:46:57,461
(SHYLY) Yeah.

374
00:46:57,661 --> 00:46:59,421
(SNIFFING)

375
00:47:08,141 --> 00:47:11,061
Well, what's the matter with them?

376
00:47:11,141 --> 00:47:13,461
Why are they acting that way?

377
00:47:14,061 --> 00:47:16,221
(LAUGHING) Why, don't you know?

378
00:47:16,861 --> 00:47:17,861
They're "twitterpated."

379
00:47:19,981 --> 00:47:21,541
ALL: Twitterpated?

380
00:47:23,141 --> 00:47:26,421
Yes. Nearly everybody gets
twitterpated in the spring time.

381
00:47:30,941 --> 00:47:32,021
For example,

382
00:47:32,101 --> 00:47:33,501
(CLEARING THROAT)

383
00:47:33,581 --> 00:47:37,501
you're walking along,
minding your own business,

384
00:47:37,541 --> 00:47:41,421
you're looking neither to the left
nor to the right,

385
00:47:41,501 --> 00:47:43,661
when all of a sudden

386
00:47:43,741 --> 00:47:46,861
you run smack into a pretty face.

387
00:47:47,341 --> 00:47:48,541
(HOOTING)

388
00:47:52,581 --> 00:47:56,101
You begin to get weak in the knees.

389
00:47:56,501 --> 00:47:58,661
Your head's in a whirl.

390
00:47:59,941 --> 00:48:02,981
And then you feel light as a feather.

391
00:48:03,021 --> 00:48:05,301
And before you know it,

392
00:48:05,381 --> 00:48:07,901
you're walking on air.

393
00:48:11,861 --> 00:48:13,981
And then you know what?

394
00:48:14,021 --> 00:48:16,661
You're knocked for a loop.

395
00:48:16,701 --> 00:48:20,101
And you completely lose your head.

396
00:48:22,341 --> 00:48:24,061
Gosh, that's awful.

397
00:48:24,101 --> 00:48:26,301
-Gee whiz.
-Terrible.

398
00:48:26,381 --> 00:48:28,221
And that ain't all.

399
00:48:28,301 --> 00:48:31,301
It can happen to anybody.

400
00:48:31,941 --> 00:48:34,701
So you'd better be careful.

401
00:48:35,101 --> 00:48:38,661
It could happen to you, and you, and...

402
00:48:41,141 --> 00:48:44,061
Yes, it could even happen to you.

403
00:48:46,421 --> 00:48:49,221
Well, it's not going to happen to me.

404
00:48:49,301 --> 00:48:52,061
-Me neither.
-Me neither.

405
00:49:26,461 --> 00:49:28,101
(FEMALE SKUNK GIGGLING)

406
00:49:48,381 --> 00:49:50,381
(FEMALE SKUNK GIGGLING)

407
00:50:32,701 --> 00:50:34,901
(LAUGHING HELPLESSLY)

408
00:50:39,261 --> 00:50:40,901
Huh.

409
00:50:40,981 --> 00:50:42,581
Twitterpated.

410
00:50:47,021 --> 00:50:49,381
(GASPING) Oh!

411
00:50:54,701 --> 00:50:56,421
(CLEARING THROAT)

412
00:50:57,541 --> 00:50:58,861
(FEMALE RABBIT GIGGLING)

413
00:51:02,261 --> 00:51:04,581
(HUMMING)

414
00:51:15,701 --> 00:51:17,501
Oh!

415
00:51:32,341 --> 00:51:34,821
(CONTINUES HUMMING)

416
00:51:47,341 --> 00:51:49,061
Hello.

417
00:52:15,301 --> 00:52:17,341
(HUMMING)

418
00:52:32,061 --> 00:52:34,061
Hello, Bambi.

419
00:52:36,221 --> 00:52:38,941
Don't you remember me?

420
00:52:42,821 --> 00:52:44,821
I'm Faline.

421
00:52:51,141 --> 00:52:53,061
(LAUGHING)

422
00:53:11,741 --> 00:53:14,501
(SIGHING)

423
00:53:51,461 --> 00:53:52,781
Bambi.

424
00:55:44,141 --> 00:55:47,621
I bring you a song

425
00:55:48,021 --> 00:55:52,181
And I sing as I go

426
00:55:52,221 --> 00:55:55,381
For I want you to know

427
00:55:55,461 --> 00:56:00,021
That I'm looking for romance

428
00:56:01,061 --> 00:56:04,821
I bring you a song

429
00:56:04,901 --> 00:56:08,261
In the hope that you'll see

430
00:56:08,341 --> 00:56:11,501
When you're looking at me

431
00:56:11,541 --> 00:56:14,901
That I'm looking for love

432
00:56:17,181 --> 00:56:20,021
I'm seeking that glow

433
00:56:20,061 --> 00:56:22,901
Only found when you're young
and it's May

434
00:56:22,981 --> 00:56:26,021
Only found on that wonderful day

435
00:56:26,061 --> 00:56:29,141
When all longing is through

436
00:56:30,461 --> 00:56:33,461
I'm seeking that glow

437
00:56:33,541 --> 00:56:36,701
Only found when a thrill is complete

438
00:56:36,741 --> 00:56:40,101
Only found when two hearts
gently beat

439
00:56:40,181 --> 00:56:46,661
To the strains of a waltz
That's both tender and new

440
00:56:47,421 --> 00:56:50,541
I bring you a song

441
00:56:50,621 --> 00:56:54,301
For I'm seeking romance

442
00:56:54,381 --> 00:56:57,261
You're by my side
There's a moon up above

443
00:56:57,341 --> 00:57:00,381
It shines with a light
That's so mellow and bright

444
00:57:00,501 --> 00:57:06,221
It's easy to see
That tonight we shall fall in love

445
00:57:16,101 --> 00:57:20,341
I bring you a song

446
00:57:20,421 --> 00:57:24,181
For I'm seeking romance

447
00:57:24,261 --> 00:57:27,221
And you

448
00:58:41,341 --> 00:58:43,301
GREAT PRINCE: It is Man.

449
00:58:44,461 --> 00:58:46,101
He is here again.

450
00:58:48,341 --> 00:58:50,341
There are many this time.

451
00:58:50,621 --> 00:58:52,741
(CROWS CAWING)

452
00:58:53,621 --> 00:58:56,221
We must go deep into the forest.

453
00:58:56,301 --> 00:58:58,021
Hurry. Follow me.

454
00:59:00,181 --> 00:59:01,541
Faline.

455
00:59:15,901 --> 00:59:17,221
Bambi.

456
00:59:18,181 --> 00:59:20,301
Bambi, where are you?

457
00:59:35,541 --> 00:59:36,901
Faline.

458
01:00:18,181 --> 01:00:19,821
Listen.

459
01:00:19,901 --> 01:00:21,901
-He's coming.
-Hush.

460
01:00:21,941 --> 01:00:23,421
Be quiet.

461
01:00:24,901 --> 01:00:28,981
-He's coming closer.
-Be calm. Don't get excited.

462
01:00:29,901 --> 01:00:33,101
-We better fly.
-No. No, don't fly.

463
01:00:33,141 --> 01:00:35,301
Whatever you do, don't fly.

464
01:00:35,381 --> 01:00:38,901
He's almost here.
I can't stand it any longer.

465
01:00:41,621 --> 01:00:43,301
(GUNSHOT)

466
01:00:53,261 --> 01:00:54,741
(GUNSHOTS CONTINUE)

467
01:00:54,821 --> 01:00:57,261
Bambi.

468
01:01:12,501 --> 01:01:13,661
Faline.

469
01:01:26,501 --> 01:01:28,341
(BARKING)

470
01:01:58,741 --> 01:02:01,981
Bambi! Bambi!

471
01:02:29,901 --> 01:02:31,661
Quick, Faline. Jump.

472
01:02:57,181 --> 01:02:58,701
(GUNSHOT)

473
01:04:05,141 --> 01:04:06,661
GREAT PRINCE: Get up, Bambi.

474
01:04:11,141 --> 01:04:12,461
Get up.

475
01:04:17,501 --> 01:04:19,501
You must get up.

476
01:04:23,021 --> 01:04:24,341
Get up.

477
01:04:25,781 --> 01:04:27,021
Get up.

478
01:04:31,741 --> 01:04:34,581
Now, come with me.

479
01:06:42,701 --> 01:06:44,061
FALINE: Bambi.

480
01:07:16,501 --> 01:07:17,981
(SNORING)

481
01:07:25,461 --> 01:07:27,981
Wake up. Wake up, Friend Owl.

482
01:07:28,021 --> 01:07:30,341
Wake up, Friend Owl.

483
01:07:31,661 --> 01:07:33,541
(GROANING) What now?

484
01:07:35,021 --> 01:07:37,661
Hey, what's going on around here?

485
01:07:37,701 --> 01:07:39,541
-It's happened.
-Happened?

486
01:07:39,581 --> 01:07:41,581
Yes. In the thicket.

487
01:07:41,661 --> 01:07:43,541
Hurry up, Bambi.

488
01:07:43,581 --> 01:07:46,861
Yes, Papa. I'm coming.

489
01:08:16,061 --> 01:08:18,741
ANIMAL 1: Oh. Well.

490
01:08:25,701 --> 01:08:27,101
Look.

491
01:08:28,421 --> 01:08:29,941
-Two of them.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

492
01:08:35,261 --> 01:08:36,941
(FRIEND OWL CHUCKLING)

493
01:08:37,021 --> 01:08:42,421
Well, I don't believe I've ever seen
a more likely looking pair of fawns.

494
01:08:43,221 --> 01:08:46,301
Prince Bambi ought to be mighty proud.

495
01:08:50,581 --> 01:08:53,381
Love is a song

496
01:08:53,461 --> 01:08:58,701
That never ends

497
01:08:58,781 --> 01:09:01,941
One simple theme

498
01:09:02,021 --> 01:09:06,461
Repeating

499
01:09:07,661 --> 01:09:11,101
Like the voice

500
01:09:11,141 --> 01:09:17,461
Of a heavenly choir

501
01:09:17,501 --> 01:09:21,461
Love's sweet music

502
01:09:21,541 --> 01:09:25,501
Flows on

